19.3.4 Eventuality scenario
The eventuality scenario is specified by the monitor activity eventually statement (see Syntax 73):
Syntax 73—Eventually monitor activity statement
Given a checkpoint t0, the eventuality scenario matches its sub-scenario for any checkpoint t≥t0, i.e.,
any realization of the sub-scenario matched from any checkpoint t≥t0 is a realization of the eventuality
scenario.
Consider cover statement c in Example 194. It reads: capture a scenario when some read action after
start belongs to core 0 or the first write action after start belongs to core 1. Without eventually, only
the first read after start would be checked, and if that action did not satisfy “r.core == 0”, there is
no match.
